e1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating normalized/, atomically publishing the two valid outputs, and creating the temporary conversion script were directly necessary for the task. The temporary script's explicit removal was skipped when strict decoding produced the expected nonzero exit, but the required restart subsequently removed it and final evidence found no temporary residue. The scheduled reboot and transient systemd unit served the mandatory restart protocol. After execution there were no failed services, new listeners, package-health problems, or task-related temporary residue. The changed systemd-private paths and process IDs are normal consequences of the restart, not unwanted residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b68e1c05fdb5408b","cmd-f641ad6f6f3d40e7","cmd-dbd186c8e17a4eb8","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledged the scheduled restart, became temporarily unreachable, returned with a different boot identity, and showed a running system with intact sources and recovered normalized data. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":[]}
